import{_ as t,o as n,c as a,a5 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BfQ7H7Qx.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Test plan","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/neo4j-all-nodes/test.md","filePath":"feature/neo4j-all-nodes/test.md"}'),r={name:"feature/neo4j-all-nodes/test.md"};function i(o,e,d,l,c,p){return n(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="test-plan" tabindex="-1">Test plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#test-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Test plan&quot;">​</a></h1><p>AI: empty page graph=null, deterministic elementId cursor no duplicates across static pages, disconnected/custom-label/brand nodes visible; only page edges with real ids; maxEdges truncation truthful; unknown properties excluded; all scope expands any relationship but public queries retain their existing predicates. No mock client accepted, DB errors -&gt;503, missing expanded root -&gt;404. Search/cursor parameterized, invalid lengths/limits/scope rejected. Business: requireAdmin before upstream call, encoded query/cursor preserve reserved characters, limits/scope rejected before upstream, failures propagated, existing public callers unchanged. Reuse AdminTrendGraphServiceTest. Web: schemas accept empty/all/custom labels and reject invalid topology; All mode shows isolated/posts, pagination switches whole page/reset on search, current page + link hint explicit; keyboard labels, loading/error/retry/empty. npm run ci; no new tests in src, no local-only artifacts committed. No production DB/AWS calls, deployment/restart/crawl or shared database mutation. Existing uncommitted real-data fixes preserved. Results — 2026-11-15:</p><ul><li>AI focused suite: 36 passed, including selection bounds, unknown-label projection, mock-driver rejection, internal auth, persistence and board regressions. Full app + modified test flake8 passed.</li><li>Business focused tests: 18 passed (8 graph service + 10 trend controller), BUILD SUCCESS. New coverage: admin denied never calls upstream, search/cursor reserved characters encoded, invalid bounds/scope rejected, all scope explicit and old expand signature defaults public. Existing JaCoCo stale-data warnings remain; pom unchanged.</li><li>Web npm run ci passed: lint, type-check, build/prerender. Four focused server-render/schema checks passed: All mode renders isolated/CrawledPost/custom nodes at initial zoom; default public behavior unchanged; empty page accepted; bad cursor and dangling-edge topology rejected. QA test source lives only in ignored keep-local-only; temporary tests/unit runner file removed.</li><li>Actual Cypher smoke: Neo4j 5.26 Docker container created for this task on a dedicated internal network. Separate Python image ran modified service source with no .env loading or shared credentials. Fixture: 7 nodes including isolated/private/custom/legacy/label-less numeric-name nodes; 3 keyset pages returned each node exactly once. Search, empty page, induced edges, edge cap/truncation, safe properties and public/all expansion isolation passed. Fixture emitted normal unknown-property/deprecated-subquery notifications. QA container and network deleted after test.</li><li>Public vocabulary, trend privacy predicate and allowed public relationships unchanged. All-mode projection still omits non-allowlisted sensitive properties. Both modes use real read-only driver and timeouts.</li><li>No live-browser interaction or production DB content verification performed; SVG rendering was exercised directly. No production deploy/restart, AWS access, shared DB mutation, commit or push.</li></ul><h2 id="large-graph-acceptance" tabindex="-1">Large graph acceptance <a class="header-anchor" href="#large-graph-acceptance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Large graph acceptance&quot;">​</a></h2><p>API: edge keyset monotonic, no duplicate/repeated cursor, cross-node-batch edges retrieved, both endpoint search predicates honored, no writes/mock fallback, empty page completes, invalid limits/cursors/auth rejected. Loader: accumulate &gt;200 nodes; keep edges until both endpoints present; abort/error retains progress, retry resumes, stale responses ignored, no automatic infinite scan. Loaded counts reflect actual unique records; filtered pending endpoints reported. Reset aborts old scan. Layout: no overlapping placements, isolated group separate on explicit rearrange, initial positions deterministic and existing coordinates unchanged on incremental loads. Overview no O(n^2) global force pass. Canvas culls offscreen marks, minimizes labels/links, selection available by keyboard list as well as canvas, fit/full-screen/responsive theme support. Legacy SVG/trend limits unchanged. Verification: existing tracked unit tests where suitable, ignored QA tests/scripts only (no new src tests), isolated Neo4j fixture beyond 200 nodes, full Web ci and focused Business/AI. No deploy/shared DB writes/crawl.</p><p>Large-graph upgrade results — 2026-11-15:</p><ul><li>AI focused regression suite: 36 passed; app flake8 passed. Business focused suite: 21 passed, BUILD SUCCESS; existing stale JaCoCo execution-data warnings remain, pom unchanged.</li><li>Final Web npm run ci passed (lint, type-check, build and 105-route prerender). Existing repository lint/chunk-size warnings remain. Vietnamese/English admin JSON has no duplicate keys.</li><li>Seven ignored QA unit tests passed: 600-node accumulation, cross-batch links, retry at same cursor, aborted response isolation, repeated-cursor rejection, public cap retained, deterministic/non-overlapping 3,000-node layout and incremental coordinate stability. Temporary tests/unit QA file removed.</li><li>Actual Neo4j 5.26 QA: isolated Docker/internal network, 600 fixture nodes and 600 real relationships. Three 200-node pages and two 400/200-edge pages returned unique complete records; 551 cross-node-batch relationships retained. Empty/search endpoint filtering passed; includeEdges=false skipped induced edges. Container/network removed after testing, no shared DB used.</li><li>Browser QA used the actual Overview component in an explicitly labelled, ignored fixture harness, not production data: 600 nodes/390 links loaded; pause at 400 nodes then resume to completion; rearrange, light/dark themes, fullscreen enter/exit and keyboard search/selection passed. At 390x844 viewport, document width stayed within viewport. Dedicated QA browser closed.</li><li>Removed CI-generated SEO/blog-index diffs. QA fixtures, logs and screenshots stay ignored/local-only. No new tracked test files. No commit/push or production deployment.</li></ul><p>Limits: all-node mode no longer caps the accumulated scene at 200; individual requests remain bounded at 200 nodes/400 relationships. Full scans are not a transaction-consistent snapshot while DB writers run; changed/missing endpoints are counted and reported. Browser memory and render time still depend on total graph size; 3,000-node layout checks do not prove unlimited-scale performance. Layout groups connected components visually only; it does not infer semantics or merge DB nodes. Existing public/trend SVG scope and limits remain unchanged. Restart local AI/Business to serve the new edge endpoint when reviewing against live local data.</p><h2 id="overview-interaction-parity-acceptance" tabindex="-1">Overview interaction parity acceptance <a class="header-anchor" href="#overview-interaction-parity-acceptance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Overview interaction parity acceptance&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In ignored browser fixture: select and drag a known node at non-unit zoom; its center and incident edge must move by pointer delta while another node/background stays fixed; click must not move it. Progressive append retains manual position; release restores automatic layout. Background drag pans scene. Double click expands once; controls show errors/loading via existing workspace. First all-mode node can hide; category filter can hide/restore all matching nodes including first. Highlight button changes connected-node rendering, edge-label toggle is connected. Selected-node move buttons and keyboard work; cancel/lost pointer capture stops drag. Public SVG unchanged. Verify light/dark, narrow viewport and vi/en; full Web CI. Browser results (2026-11-15): ignored real-component fixture passed node drag +72/+36 CSS px while another node stayed fixed; unpin restored automatic position. Manual position survived progressive load 200 -&gt; 600 nodes. Background pan moved scene +32/+20 px. Double-click expanded exactly once (fixture counter attached to actual service override); move button +24 px and Shift+Down +60 px passed. Category filter 600 -&gt; 450 -&gt; 600 and first/root hide 600 -&gt; 599 -&gt; reset 600 passed. Highlight and edge-label controls share workspace state. Light/dark screenshots inspected; 390px viewport no horizontal overflow. Fixed single-click inspector geometry shift interfering with double-click by deferring single-click selection 250ms and cancelling it on double click/drag. Focused ESLint passed; vi/en graph keys parallel without duplicates. Full Web npm run ci passed (0 lint errors, 194 existing warnings; type-check, production build and 105-route prerender successful). Existing chunk-size/plugin-timing warnings remain. QA browser closed and generated SEO/blog-index diffs restored. No backend/DB changes in this follow-up, no commit/push.</p><h2 id="rank-one-scan-acceptance" tabindex="-1">Rank-one scan acceptance <a class="header-anchor" href="#rank-one-scan-acceptance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Rank-one scan acceptance&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Seed: newer daily all snapshot beats old high-score trend; same-day score desc/id tie-break matches rank one, omit private/category-specific/synthetic seed. Neighbor reads: both directions/custom rels, self/cycles, cross-frontier duplicates dedup client-side, &gt;200 degree paginated without loss, q applies both endpoints, invalid cursor/frontier rejected, admin/internal auth required. BFS: root appears first; hop1 fully traversed before hop2 processing; queue each node once; disconnected component/isolated fallback completes full static DB, no arbitrary scene/depth cap. Abort/error/repeated cursor retains progress and retries same request; no ranked root and empty DB truthful. Browser auto-start, root selection, pause/resume and interactions still work; vi/en, light/dark; CI. Results (2026-11-15):</p><ul><li>Eight ignored Web BFS QA unit checks passed: root-first layers, full disconnected fallback, &gt;200 degree pagination/50-center chunks, cycles/self loops, error retry at same cursor, abort isolation, repeated-cursor rejection, empty/no-rank fallback and pause/resume controller. Temporary test runner removed.</li><li>Real Neo4j 5.26 isolated internal-network Docker test passed: newest daily top score selected over older higher score, brand/private and category-specific candidates excluded from seed; rank root had 611 incident relationships over 4 pages including parallel/self loops. BFS plus keyset seeds visited all 610 nodes/616 relationships across 7 components and hop 3. Every node expanded once, q checks both endpoints and invalid cursor/frontier rejected. QA container/network removed.</li><li>Business focused tests: 24 passed, BUILD SUCCESS; authorization precedes upstream, bounded frontier rejects bad/duplicate ids, cursor/body preserved. Existing JaCoCo stale execution-data warnings remain; pom unchanged.</li><li>AI regression 36 passed, 4 existing utcnow deprecation warnings. App flake8 passed.</li><li>Web UI fixture auto-scanned to 600 nodes/390 edges, deepest hop 39 and 210 components. Pause/resume retained progress; root rank-one selection remained; auto-fit completion only if camera/node position has not been manually changed. Fixture took longer than the browser test&#39;s initial 30s wait while CI ran, then completed normally. No duration/unlimited-size performance guarantee.</li><li>Final Web npm run ci passed: lint (0 errors, 194 existing warnings), TypeScript, production build and 105-route prerender. vi/en keys including phases are parallel with no duplicates; light/dark reviewed and 390px viewport no horizontal overflow. Post-load node move/pin still works. Browser QA closed, generated SEO/blog-index diffs restored. No shared DB writes, production access/deployment, commit or push.</li></ul><h2 id="post-visibility-right-pan-tests" tabindex="-1">Post visibility/right pan tests <a class="header-anchor" href="#post-visibility-right-pan-tests" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Post visibility/right pan tests&quot;">​</a></h2><p>On ignored real-component fixture: switch hides all CrawledPost nodes/incident edges and restores full counts; collection scan/loaded counts unaffected. Filter remains in toolbar even if no posts loaded. Right drag moves every node equally; right drag starting on node also pans rather than pinning it; right click does not alter selected node or open native context menu. Left background drag leaves camera unchanged; left node drag still changes just that node. Touch background pan and keyboard remain. vi/en, light/dark, mobile width; Web CI. Browser QA results (2026-11-15, ignored fixture only, no DB/API access): switch 4 nodes/4 edges -&gt; 2 nodes/1 edge -&gt; 4/4; right background drag moved all nodes +36/+22px; right drag starting on node moved all +28/+16px without pinning; left background drag left camera unchanged; left node drag moved only that node +40/+24px. Native context menu prevented. Real CDP touch drag moved all nodes +24/+18px; Shift+Right moved selected node +60px and retained neighbor. Shared switch has associated label; Vietnamese/English keys parallel, no duplicates; light/dark captured and 390px layout inspected without horizontal overflow. QA browser closed. Focused ESLint and full Web npm run ci passed (0 errors, 194 existing warnings; TypeScript, production build and 105-route prerender successful). Generated SEO/blog-index diffs restored. Public SVG/backend unchanged; no shared DB writes or new tracked tests. No commit/push.</p><h2 id="relationship-context-tests" tabindex="-1">Relationship context tests <a class="header-anchor" href="#relationship-context-tests" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Relationship context tests&quot;">​</a></h2><p>On ignored component fixture with an unrelated edge, compare Canvas edge strokes before/after selecting node: total drawn edge count unchanged; incident strokes use accent/thicker width, unrelated stroke remains visible and can be selected. Turning emphasis off keeps all edges. Explicit post/type filters still remove their edges. Browser QA passed with 4/4 relationships retained: selecting root highlighted 3 in accent/thicker stroke and kept 1 dimmed visible. Disabling emphasis retained 4/4; the unrelated edge e2 remained clickable and opened its properties. Light/dark captured; light screenshot inspected. Focused ESLint and npm run type-check passed. vi/en label updated, no new tracked test files. QA browser closed; no DB/API writes or commit/push.</p><p>Final pre-commit verification (2026-11-15): full Web npm run ci passed on final selection-context changes, including lint, TypeScript, production build and 105-route prerender. Existing lint/chunk-size warnings remain. Business/AI sources unchanged since focused 24/36 passing checks and isolated Neo4j traversal verification. Only graph source, existing tracked Business test updates and feature docs included; QA fixtures, clean scripts, database backup and generated SEO/blog-index changes excluded.</p>',18)])])}const h=t(r,[["render",i]]);export{g as __pageData,h as default};
